text.paragraph:
Azithromycin for oral suspension USP is a macrolide antibacterial drug indicated for the treatment of patients with mild to moderate infections caused by susceptible strains of the designated microorganisms in the specific conditions listed below. Recommended dosages and durations of therapy in adult and pediatric patient populations vary in these indications. [see 



                        Dosage and Administration (2)
                     ]

Azithromycin has been shown to be active against most isolates of the following microorganisms, both in vitro and in clinical infections. [see 



                              Indications and Usage (1)
                           ]
